|~ `::bind`, the step that declares a name, and what is declared under
   it: its constructor and the refusals of a declaration.
   The decisions it exists for: [D114]. ~|

:bind
  |~~ A declaration, `:name body`, names a value for the steps after it,
      in the scope where it stands:
      `{:qty 2 :price 3} | :r it | get /qty | mul (r | get /price)` keeps the
      record for a later step and answers `6`. The value in the pipe
      passes on unchanged; a group, a part of a literal and a quote a
      word runs each close the names declared inside, and a name is
      declared once in its scope.

      In a quote the step is a record, `~(:x 1) | first` answering
      `::bind{:name :x :body 1}`: `:name` the keyword or tag it binds,
      `:docs` its pages and `:body` the step of its body.
      ::link~(::binding | doc) ::link~(::qlang/names | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The record of a declaration, `:name`, `:docs` and `:body`,
            built into its step, which reads back as itself.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotSchemaError
        |~~ A `::bind` is a map of `:name`, a keyword, `:docs`, a vector
            of docs, and `:body`, a step, and `:field` names the field
            that does not fit: a tag is no name a declaration binds, and
            the body is the step a quote holds, so the declaration
            `:inc add 1` is
            `{:name :inc :body (~(add 1) | first)} | tag ::bind`.
            ::link~(::bind | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :ReadBackDiffersError
        |~~ The `::bind` prints as text that reads back as another step,
            and `:printed` is that text: a declaration with neither a body
            nor a page prints as the bare keyword, which reads back as the
            keyword, and a body that is a doc prints where a page of the
            declaration stands, and reads back as its page. A declaration
            binds a body or a page, and a doc bound as the value is the
            body of a group.
            ::link~(::bind | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :NounNotDeclaredError
        |~~ A name with a path is declared under the noun its path names
            before its last name, and that noun is declared before it, so
            whether the noun is a kind, which the verbs under it serve, is
            known where they are declared: `:name` holds the name and
            `:noun` the noun no declaration made. The noun is declared
            first, a kind by its chain or by its page alone, and the names
            under it after.
            ::link~(::bind | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :NounNotDeclaredError/name
        |~~ The name declared. ~~|
        ::keyword
    | carries :NounNotDeclaredError/noun
        |~~ The noun its path names, which no declaration names. ~~|
        ::tag
    | throws :WrittenOutsideItsChainError
        |~~ A kind and a function hold what they are in the chains that
            build them: an invariant is written
            `| holds :NotPositiveError |~~ … ~~| ~(gt 0)`, the constructor
            of a kind `| impl ~(…)`, and an input of a word `| takes …`,
            its answer `| returns …` and its subject `| on …`. Declared by
            a name, an invariant holds of no value, and a constructor
            under a label, or an input, an answer or a subject under a
            word, is read by no call, so the declaration is refused,
            `:name` naming it and `:noun` the label or the word it is
            under. A page and a law are declared by a name under any of
            them.
            ::link~(::kind | doc) ::link~(::fn | doc)
            ::link~(::bind | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/name
        |~~ The name declared outside the chain that holds what it
            declares.
        ~~|
        ::keyword
    | carries :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/noun
        |~~ The label or the word the name is declared under. ~~|
        ::tag
    | throws :NameDeclaredTwiceError
        |~~ A name is declared once in a scope: the steps of a pipeline
            that the pipe or the fail track joins share one scope, and a
            declaration of a name one of them declared before is refused
            where it stands, `:name` the name. A group, an element, a
            modifier and a quote open scopes of their own, where a name of
            the scope around them is shadowed, so a second value takes
            another name or a group of its own, `(:k 2 | k)`. The body of
            a word runs in a scope its call opens with `args` and each
            input, so a step of the body declares none of them again: the
            body reads an input by its name, and a value of its own takes
            another. An address the root holds is declared once at all: a
            reader extends a noun of the root by a name of its own,
            `:vec/second ~(get /1)`, and replaces none of its names, and a
            source of the root that declares a name the root holds is
            refused.
            ::link~(::bind | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :NameDeclaredTwiceError/name
        |~~ The name declared again. ~~|
        ::keyword
    | proves :holdsTheNameAndTheBody
        |~~ A declaration holds its name and its body. ~~|
        ~(~(:inc add 1) | first | get [/name /body/name] | eq [:inc :add])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesDocsThatAreNoDocs
        |~~ Docs that are no vector of docs are refused, `:field` naming
            them.
        ~~|
        ~(::bind{:name :inc :docs [1]} !| [type (get /field)] | eq [::bind/PayloadNotSchemaError :docs])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesATagForAName
        |~~ A tag is no name a declaration binds. ~~|
        ~({:name ::Box :body 1} | tag ::bind
          !| [type (get /field)] | eq [::bind/PayloadNotSchemaError :name])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/buildsTheDeclarationOfABody
        |~~ A keyword and the step a quote holds build the declaration. ~~|
        ~({:name :inc :body (~(add 1) | first)} | tag ::bind
          | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~(:inc add 1))
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/refusesABindOfNothing
        |~~ A bind with neither a body nor docs prints as a bare name,
            which reads back as another step.
        ~~|
        ~(::bind{:name :inc} !| [type (get /printed)] | eq [::bind/ReadBackDiffersError ":inc"])
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/refusesABodyThatIsADoc
        |~~ A doc as the body reads back as the page of the declaration. ~~|
        ~({:name :k :body (~(|~~ x ~~|) | first)} | tag ::bind
          !| type | eq ::bind/ReadBackDiffersError)
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/bindsADocInAGroup
        |~~ A doc in a group is the value a declaration binds. ~~|
        ~(:k (|~~ x ~~|) | k | content | eq " x ")
    | proves :NounNotDeclaredError/refusesANameUnderNoNoun
        |~~ A name under a noun no declaration made is refused, naming the
            noun.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box/area ~(1) !| [type (get /noun)] | eq [::bind/NounNotDeclaredError ::Box])
    | proves :NounNotDeclaredError/takesANameUnderADeclaredNoun
        |~~ A name under a noun declared before it runs on the noun's
            values.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/area ~(1) | ::Box{} | area | eq 1)
    | proves :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/refusesAnInvariantDeclaredBare
        |~~ An invariant declared by a bare name holds of no value. ~~|
        ~(:Positive ::holds~(gt 0) !| [type (get /name)] | eq [::bind/WrittenOutsideItsChainError :Positive])
    | proves :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/refusesAnInvariantUnderALabel
        |~~ An invariant declared by a name under a label is refused; the
            chain of the kind writes it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Pos |~~ A positive number. ~~| | :Pos/NotPositiveError ::holds~(gt 0)
          !| [type (get /name) (get /noun)]
          |  eq [::bind/WrittenOutsideItsChainError :Pos/NotPositiveError ::Pos])
    | proves :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/refusesAConstructorUnderALabel
        |~~ A constructor declared by a name under a label is refused. ~~|
        ~(:Pos |~~ A positive number. ~~| | :Pos/construct ~(add 0) !| type | eq ::bind/WrittenOutsideItsChainError)
    | proves :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/refusesAnInputUnderAWord
        |~~ An input declared by a name under a word is refused; the chain
            of the function takes it.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus ~(add 1) | :number/plus/by /0 !| type | eq ::bind/WrittenOutsideItsChainError)
    | proves :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/refusesTheAnswerOfAWord
        |~~ The answer of a word declared by a name is refused. ~~|
        ~(:number/half ~(div 2) | :number/half/answer ::number !| type | eq ::bind/WrittenOutsideItsChainError)
    | proves :WrittenOutsideItsChainError/takesAPageAndALaw
        |~~ A page and a law are declared by a name under a kind. ~~|
        ~(:Pos |~~ A positive number. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The number. ~~| ::number)
          | :Pos/note |~~ A note. ~~|
          | :Pos/holdsFive ::law~(::Pos(5) | payload | eq 5)
          | ::Pos
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesASecondDeclaration
        |~~ A name declared again in its scope is refused. ~~|
        ~(:k 1 | :k 2 !| [type (get /name)] | eq [::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError :k])
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/letsAGroupDeclareAgain
        |~~ A group declares in a scope of its own, so it may name a name
            again.
        ~~|
        ~(:k 1 | (:k 2 | k) | eq 2)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/letsAnElementDeclareAgain
        |~~ A declaration inside an element stays in it. ~~|
        ~(:k 1 | [(:k 2 | k) k] | eq [2 1])
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/letsAModifierDeclareAgain
        |~~ A declaration inside a modifier stays in it. ~~|
        ~(:k 1 | 5 | add (:k 2 | k) | eq 7)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/letsAQuoteDeclareAgain
        |~~ A quote declares in a scope of its own. ~~|
        ~(:k 1 | apply ~(:k 2 | k) | eq 2)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesAPartDeclaredInTheBody
        |~~ The recipe of a word declares none of its inputs again. ~~|
        ~(:number/m (::fn | takes :x |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(:x 3 | add x)) | 1 | m 2 !| [type (get /name)] | eq [::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError :x])
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesANameTheRootHolds
        |~~ A reader declares no name the root holds. ~~|
        ~(:vec/count ~(0) !| type | eq ::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/extendsANounOfTheRoot
        |~~ A reader extends a noun of the root by a name of its own. ~~|
        ~(:vec/second ~(get /1) | [1 2] | second | eq 2)
    | impl ::builtin{}

